-wrap edit, after which the spec's four files were rerun and still passed.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- **`pyproject.toml`**: `condense-json>=1.1`. The installed `.venv` already has 1.1.\n- **`llm/migrations.py`**: `m027_turns_response_json` adds a nullable `turns.response_json` column.\n- **`llm/logs.py`**:\n  - Added `_payload_replacements`, `condense_payload`, `resolve_payload`, `_model_json_replacements`, and `TURN_TOOLS_SQL`, following the spec's rules.\n  - `LogStore.log` stores the condensed payload on the turn.\n  - Added `LogStore.turn_response_json` and `_turn_tool_pairs`.\n  - `llm logs` rows now resolve `response_json` via `_resolve_response_json`, which returns `None` on `UncondenseError` so one broken payload doesn't fail the listing.\n- **`llm/default_plugins/openai_models.py`**: `Responses` and `AsyncResponses` remember each streamed reasoning event by item id. After `response.completed`, they yield a refresh event carrying the final `encrypted_content`, so the stored part and `response_json` agree. The shared helper is `_reasoning_refresh_events`.\n\nNot done:\n- Black and ruff are listed in the project's dev dependencies but aren't installed in `.venv`, so I didn't run them. I checked added lines by hand for length and wrapped the one over 88 characters.\n- I didn't commit. `SPEC.md` is still untracked and I left it that way.", "ttft_ms": 1481, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 238214, "uuid": "e6d0c04e-fd6a-45e5-9ebe-2fa612b70285", "ttft_stream_ms": 1290, "time_to_request_ms": 233, "first_content_frame_ms": 1291, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
